+/**
+ * Rebinds this render session's owner thread to the calling thread.
+ *
+ * A session's owner is the thread that attached it, which suits an embedder
+ * that controls its own threads. Two shapes do not fit that. A host with
+ * managed concurrency (a Dart isolate, a Go goroutine, a .NET task) can resume
+ * on a different pool thread between two calls, through no action of the
+ * caller. And a host that renders on a display-paced callback thread while
+ * driving the map from elsewhere has to hand the session between the two,
+ * because every session entry point is owner-thread checked.
+ *
+ * Both are the same operation: re-home the affinity to the thread that is
+ * actually about to call. This does nothing else, so the map, the runtime and
+ * any other session keep the owners they had.
+ *
+ * Contract:
+ * - No call on this session may be in flight, on any thread. Callers that
+ *   hand a session back and forth must serialize the handover themselves.
+ * - Backend-bound state is made current per call, inside the graphics backend
+ *   scope each entry point opens, so no GPU context travels with the session.
+ *
+ * Returns:
+ * - MLN_STATUS_OK on success, including when already bound to the caller.
+ * - MLN_STATUS_INVALID_ARGUMENT when session is null or not a live handle.
+ * - MLN_STATUS_NATIVE_ERROR when an internal exception is converted to status.
+ */
+MLN_API mln_status
+mln_render_session_rebind_thread(mln_render_session session) MLN_NOEXCEPT;
+
